docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T43.log:1684:This task makes every LLM-driven consolidation proposal from T42 auditable, reproducible, and bounded. It adds the provenance record (model name + prompt hash + response hash attached to each proposal), enforces the spec's bounded-queue-with-warning behavior at the LLM-job submission point, encodes per-job-type cost and latency budgets, and publishes the budget rationale as an architecture doc the operator can consult. It also nails down the malformed/failed-response contract: prior memory MUST remain unchanged and a `ConsolidationFailed` event MUST be emitted. Without this task, T42's LLM jobs would be reproducible only by luck and budget overruns would propagate silently.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T43.log:1698:- Dependency outputs: T42 — `LlmDriver`, `LlmJobContext`, the four LLM jobs. Provenance attaches to the proposals they emit; budgets gate their `run` calls.
