docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T39.md:12:This task stands up the consolidation engine's runtime kernel and the proposal model on which every later Phase 6 job depends. It introduces the `consolidation_jobs` table from spec §Storage Design, the bounded job queue, and a strict invariant that no consolidation job — deterministic or LLM-driven — writes durable memory directly. Every job emits a `ConsolidationProposal` record that requires explicit `apply` or `reject` before any memory state changes. Without this kernel, the LLM-driven jobs in T42 would be free to silently mutate memory, violating spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties and the §Opaque Memory Mutation risk control.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T39.md:41:3. Author `consolidation/schema.sql` defining the `consolidation_jobs` table (columns: `job_id PK`, `workspace_id`, `kind`, `mode` ∈ {`synchronous_post_task`, `background`, `manual_review`, `replay`}, `status` ∈ {`queued`, `running`, `proposed`, `applied`, `rejected`, `failed`, `dropped`}, `enqueued_at`, `started_at`, `finished_at`, `proposal_id NULLABLE`, `error_kind NULLABLE`, indexes on `(workspace_id, status)` and `(kind, status)`) plus a `consolidation_proposals` table (columns: `proposal_id PK`, `job_id FK`, `target_memory_id NULLABLE`, `proposal_kind`, `prior_state JSON`, `proposed_state JSON`, `evidence JSON`, `decided_at NULLABLE`, `decision` ∈ {`pending`, `applied`, `rejected`}, `decided_by NULLABLE`).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T39.md:42:4. In `consolidation/proposal.rs`, define `pub struct ConsolidationProposal { proposal_id, job_id, target: ProposalTarget, prior_state, proposed_state, evidence }`, the `ProposalKind` enum (e.g. `CreateMemory`, `UpdateMemory`, `MarkStale`, `Supersede`, `Demote`, `Refresh`), and the `ProposalDecision` enum. Implement `apply()` and `reject()` methods that mutate `consolidation_proposals.decision`, emit a `MemoryConsolidated` event with prior + proposed state preserved, and only then call the memory store API to materialize the change. `apply` MUST be a no-op if `decision != pending`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T39.md:43:5. In `consolidation/queue.rs`, implement `BoundedJobQueue` with a configurable `max_depth` (default from `LatticeConfig`, no hard-coded literals). When `enqueue` is called and the queue is full, mark the job as `dropped` in `consolidation_jobs`, emit a `tracing::warn!` log including `workspace_id`, `kind`, and current depth, and return an `EnqueueOutcome::Dropped { reason }` — never block. Expose `depth()`, `pop()`, and `drain_for_shutdown()` for observability.
